    {
      "section": "dsh-cool-git",
      "text": "English · [中文](./README.zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Description",
      "text": "DeepSeek Harness Git plugin — adds a Git panel to the session tab bar: changes, commits, history, branches, remote sync, and merge-conflict resolution in one place, with AI-written commit messages."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Workspace-aware:** opens the repository of the current session\n- **Changes & diffs:** folder tree, staged state, and per-file diffs\n- **Commit history:** browse commits and their diffs\n- **Commit:** commit the whole tree in one click, or only what is staged — the scope is a toolbar menu choice — with AI-written messages (model and prompt configurable per workspace)\n- **Branches:** switch, create, delete (with risk marks), and merge\n- **Remote:** fetch, pull, push, publish, and one-click sync (pull, then push); a pull merges rather than rebases\n- **Merge conflicts:** a pull or branch merge that conflicts is left in the tree and resolved in the Diff pane — block by block, or one side everywhere — then marked resolved per file, or all at once"
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation",
      "text": "Use DSH's add-plugin feature and enter the package name: `dsh-cool-git`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Contributing",
      "text": "Contributions via Issues and PRs are welcome."
    },
